DAF Browser: remove allow_circular_includes_from from chrome/test (LSC mirror)

Root cause (hinge run #17, 13 Nov 2026): gn gen fails at
//chrome/test/BUILD.gn:3620 with "Usage of allow_circular_includes_from is
not allowed here". The usage sits in test("unit_tests"); on Android the
test() template expands it into a shared_library named unit_tests__library
(testing/test.gni:546), which forwards the annotation. GN validates the
EXPANDED label against allow_circular_includes_from_allowlist (.gn), and
the allowlist holds //chrome/test:unit_tests but not
//chrome/test:unit_tests__library. No Bare patch touches these files
(verified over all 298 patches); the pinned tree is pristine upstream and
the gn binary is the DEPS-pinned CIPD gn — the pinned commit is in a broken
window for Android gn gen. Upstream fixed it the same way: current main has
zero allow_circular_includes_from usages in chrome/test/BUILD.gn and none
of the five entries in build/circular_includes_untriaged.gni.

This patch removes all 11 usages from chrome/test/BUILD.gn (the failing one
is unit_tests:3620; the rest are removed in the same pass to match upstream
main) and the 5 matching allowlist entries (browser_tests,
interactive_ui_tests, test_support, test_support_ui, unit_tests).
chrome_test_utils stays. The annotation only affects `gn check`, never
compilation, so the removal cannot break the ninja build; `gn check --fix`
was not run (no checkout here) — upstream main is the reference.
